  "assessment": "Sources 1–3 show end elevations, oblique views and ground-level details of one elongated building, identified by its stacked external ramps and projecting glazed buffer. Source 4 shows the curved timber upper hall and a lower double-height workspace with a partial mezzanine. Sources 5 and 8 confirm this section; Source 6 separates the concrete frame, timber addition and lightweight enclosure; Source 7 locates floor openings and stairs. CURRENT captures the principal exterior arrangement, but the lower interior loses the source’s double-height openness. The spiral support and major interior material zones also differ. Exact dimensions and concealed connections remain uncertain; the uncut registered views cannot verify the source plans or sections.",
